1. Charter Purpose

This charter translates the Stage 1 product concept into an actionable and controlled MVP plan.

It defines what the first version of TENTORA will prove, which users and sectors it will serve, what functionality is included, what is intentionally excluded, how success will be measured, and which risks must be managed before development begins.

2. Project Purpose

The purpose of TENTORA is to create an AI-powered creative-solutions platform that gives project owners two connected ways to obtain creative work:

Design Now: select a ready interactive design, customize it quickly, and export or purchase a usable result.

Work With a Creative: define visual taste, receive up to six compatible creative or team recommendations, select the preferred option, and organize the project through delivery.

The platform is designed to reduce search time, simplify visual decisions, preserve consistency across multiple services, and connect self-service design with professional human creativity.

3. Product Definition

TENTORA begins with a project sector and service rather than an open directory of creative profiles or a long technical questionnaire.

The shared entry journey is:

Select Sector
→ Explore or Select Service
→ Choose Design Now or Work With a Creative

The two paths solve different levels of urgency and complexity while remaining connected. A user may customize a ready design first and later transfer the saved work to a compatible creative for professional development.

TENTORA is not:

A conventional freelance marketplace.

A generic template library.

A fully autonomous AI design generator.

A simple portfolio directory.

A replacement for artists and designers.

It is a structured system connecting ready interactive design, AI-assisted customization, visual taste, creative matching, and project delivery.

4. MVP Objectives

The MVP will validate the following objectives:

Build a sector-based discovery experience covering five initial sectors and their relevant creative services.

Prove the Design Now concept through a controlled set of ready interactive designs with clearly defined editable properties.

Allow a user to select, customize, preview, and export at least one valid ready-design output without specialist design knowledge.

Allow clients to select one or multiple services within one project context.

Allow clients to complete one visual taste test in under three minutes without mandatory initial registration.

Create one Main Taste Profile per project and reuse it across all selected services.

Allow an optional service-specific taste refinement without repeating the full test.

Return no more than six relevant creative or team recommendation options.

Provide curated access to approximately 30–50 creative portfolios across the five sectors.

Provide a basic project workspace for communication, references, files, feedback, milestones, and delivery tracking.

Demonstrate a handoff from a saved Design Now result to a professional creative without requiring the client to re-enter the same information.

Preserve creator attribution, customization permissions, and licensing information for every ready design included in the MVP.

