8. MVP Functional Requirements

8.1 Sector and Service Discovery

The system shall display the five approved sectors.

The system shall display relevant services and curated visual examples after a sector is selected.

The system shall provide clear access to Design Now and Work With a Creative from a selected service.

8.2 Design Now

The system shall display ready designs relevant to the selected sector and service.

The system shall identify the original creative for each ready design.

The system shall load only the editable properties permitted by the design definition.

The system shall allow the user to preview changes before export or save.

The system shall preserve the original design rules during AI-assisted actions.

The system shall store the selected design, custom properties, client content, and uploaded assets when the user saves.

The system shall support at least one validated export type for every pilot design.

8.3 Project Needs and Taste

The system shall allow one or multiple services to be added to My Project Needs.

The system shall provide one image-based taste test per project.

The system shall produce one Main Taste Profile.

The system shall apply the Main Taste Profile to all selected services by default.

The system shall allow an optional service direction through a shorter visual refinement.

The system shall not require the full taste test to be repeated for another service in the same project.

8.4 Creative DNA and Matching

The system shall store structured Creative DNA for each approved creative.

Creative DNA shall include services, sector relevance, visual attributes, and portfolio work.

The matching engine shall consider sector, services, Main Taste Profile, optional service directions, and Creative DNA.

The matching engine shall return no more than six recommendation options.

A recommendation option may represent one creative, a multidisciplinary studio, or a compatible team.

The result shall explain the major reasons for each recommendation.

8.5 Portfolio and Selection

The client shall be able to explore a recommended creative's portfolio and relevant services.

The client shall be able to save, compare, and select a preferred option.

The system shall preserve the project services and taste context during selection.

8.6 Project Workspace

The system shall create a workspace after a creative project is started.

The workspace shall store the project summary, selected services, taste direction, references, files, feedback, milestones, responsibilities, and delivery state.

The client and creative shall be able to exchange project messages and files.

8.7 Design-to-Creative Handoff

A Design Now user shall be able to select Continue With a Creative.

The system shall transfer the selected ready design, customizations, content, and assets into the project context.

The system shall avoid requesting information already stored in the design session.

8.8 Authentication

Initial sector, service, work, and ready-design exploration shall not require login.

Authentication shall be introduced progressively when an action requires persistent identity, ownership, purchase, export, or project collaboration.

