14. Assumptions and Constraints

14.1 Assumptions

A curated portfolio set can be obtained and classified for the MVP.

Ready-design contributors will provide explicit customization and licensing permissions.

Pilot outputs can use a controlled two-dimensional editor before advanced motion or 3D functionality.

Weighted tag matching is sufficient to validate the early matching experience.

Users value both immediate self-service output and access to human creative expertise.

14.2 Constraints

Development time and team capacity are limited.

The ready-design editor and AI actions must be constrained to prevent uncontrolled technical expansion.

Matching quality depends on the quality and consistency of portfolio and taste data.

The MVP will not have enough behavioural data to train a mature recommendation model.

Copyright, creator consent, licensing, and privacy requirements constrain how creative work and user data may be used.

